  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since the exponent of the binomial expression is $n=4,$ we see that the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{x}^{4},\\,{x}^{3},\\,{x}^{2},\\,{x}^{1},\\,{x}^{0}\n$$\n\nOf these, the term that returns ${x}^{2}$ is the third. So, we are looking for the third term in the binomial expansion.\n\nThe $4$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,4,6,4,1).$ Therefore, the third term in the binomial expansion is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(2x)^{2}{(-3)}^{2} & =6(4{x}^{2})(9)=216{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the expansion of $(2x-3)^{4}$ is $216.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
